<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1492 0 R
/E (Decorate the front of your cardstock. Decide where you would like your LED to light up.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [22]
>>
endobj
535 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1493 0 R
/E (Carefully poke one small hole with a sharpened pencil using a twisting motion where you want the LED to be placed. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [23]
>>
endobj
536 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1494 0 R
/E (On the back of the cardstock, draw two short horizontal lines coming out from the puncture holes. Then draw two longer lines extending straight up from the ends of the short lines. Label one side of your circuit "Short" and the other "Long.")
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [24]
>>
endobj
537 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1495 0 R
/E (Cut a strip of copper tape and apply it along the Short side. The tape should stop at the edge of the cardboard and should not extend past it.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [25]
>>
endobj
538 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1496 0 R
/E (Cut a second strip of copper tape that is longer than the first. Peel back only enough of the backing to attach the tape along your line to the edge of the cardboard, leaving the remaining backing on the extra length. Apply the tape along the Long side so the extra length extends past the edge of the cardboard. \(See blue image\))
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
539 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1497 0 R
/E (Insert the LED through the two holes from the front of the cardstock. Make sure the longer leg lays across the Long side and the shorter leg lays across the Short side.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
540 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1498 0 R
/E (Bend both LED legs flat against the back of the cardstock. Use two small pieces of tape to secure the legs in place so they line up with the copper tape. \(The tape should be placed vertically\))
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [28]
>>
endobj
541 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1499 0 R
/E (Place the coin cell battery face up on top of the end of the Short copper tape. Secure only half of the battery with one piece of tape horizontally so the other half is uncovered. \(See image below to identify the top of the battery\))
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [29]
>>
endobj
542 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1500 0 R
/E (Fold the extra length of the Long copper tape diagonally so the exposed copper touches the top of the battery. Press the copper tape against the battery to complete the circuit. The LED should light up.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [30]
>>
endobj
543 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1501 0 R
/E (If the LED does not light up, check that the battery is facing the correct direction, the LED's long and short legs are in the correct positions, and the copper tape is making good contact with both the LED legs and the battery.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [31]
>>
endobj
